// Cedar's `like`, the one string operator in the modelled subset.
//
// The pattern is evaluated by TLC, in `LikeMatches`. A TLA+ string is a sequence and TLC supports
// `Len`, `\o` and `SubSeq` on one -- only function application is missing, so a character is read
// as SubSeq(s, i, i) rather than s[i].
//
// This fixture exists to keep the answer `live`. The vacuity checker invents the values a field
// can take, so it has to invent one the pattern MATCHES; without that the guard can never be true
// and the permit reports VACUOUS -- a working rule declared inert, the one wrong answer this tool
// must not give.

@id("sell_a_prefixed")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"SellShares",
    resource
)
when { context.input.stock like "A*" };
